# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill One or two sentences: what this iPhone app does and who uses it. -->

An iPhone app in Objective-C and UIKit, with one Swift file called from Objective-C. The Xcode project is generated from `project.yml` by XcodeGen.

## Requirements

<!-- stacks:fill Xcode version, minimum iOS version, and the clang-format and XcodeGen versions this project was set up with. -->

- macOS with Xcode and an iPhone simulator runtime
- `brew install xcodegen clang-format` (and `xcbeautify` for readable build output)

## Getting started

```sh
make install   # check tools, generate the Xcode project
make ci        # lint, build, analyze, unit tests, UI smoke tests
open *.xcodeproj
```

`make help` lists every target. Set `SIMULATOR_UDID` (from `xcrun simctl list devices available`) to choose the simulator; otherwise a booted iPhone is used, then the first iPhone on the newest iOS runtime.

